	charset=us-ascii

Based on feedback from Kirk and Colin I added configuring the parser =
class name via server.properties, added some tests, and updated the docs =
to reflect this.
I find the config file name by re-parsing the command line. If anyone =
knows a better way of passing KafkaConfig to static initialization, I'd =
appreciate a nudge in the right direction. It's not the most efficient =
way of retrieving configs, but it is done only once at load time, so the =
overhead should be negligible while providing a consistent location for =
all configs. I have also left the system prop and env ways of passing =
this config in. Hopefully this is ok and is not considered a code bloat.

Thanks!
Max=20


> On Aug 29, 2024, at 10:25 AM, Maxim Fortun <max@maxf.net> wrote:
>=20
> Hi all,
> I would like to introduce a minor code change to allow custom produce =
request parsers.=20
>=20
> KIP: =
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=3D3186065=
28
> JIRA: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17348
> PR: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/16812
>=20
> There are many potential benefits for this feature. A custom produce =
request parser would allow to intercept all incoming messages before =
they get into the broker and apply broker wide logic to the messages. =
This could be a trace, a filter, a transform(such as lineage), forcing =
required headers across all messages, compression, signing, encryption, =
or any other message manipulation before it gets into the broker.=20
>=20
> Please take a look.
> Any and all feedback is greatly appreciated.
> Thanks,
> Max
>=20
>=20
>=20
>=20


