Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-17484) Logs are deleted in Kafka 1.1.1 if
 logs.segment.bytes is changed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Georgios Kousouris created KAFKA-17484:
------------------------------------------

             Summary: Logs are deleted in Kafka 1.1.1 if logs.segment.bytes=
 is changed
                 Key: KAFKA-17484
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17484
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
    Affects Versions: 1.1.1
         Environment: Kafka 1.1.1
            Reporter: Georgios Kousouris
             Fix For: 2.0.0


On Kafka 1.1.1 we have observed this unexpected behaviour. If there is a to=
pic with {{cleanup.policy=3Dcompact}}=C2=A0and the server-wide=C2=A0{{log.s=
egments.bytes}} field is modified, the compact logs are deleted.

Steps to reproduce the bug:

=C2=A0
{code:java}
1. Download the Kafka 1.1.1 zip file
$ curl -O https://archive.apache.org/dist/kafka/1.1.1/kafka_2.11-1.1.1.tgz

2. Unzip it
$ tar -xzf kafka_2.11-1.1.1.tgz

3. Start Zookeeper
$ bin/zookeeper-server-start.sh config/zookeeper.properties

4. Adjust config/server.properties with these properties
> log.retention.ms=3D10000
> log.segment.bytes=3D100

5. Create a test-topic
$ bin/kafka-topics.sh --create --zookeeper localhost:2181 --replication-fac=
tor 1 --partitions 1 --topic test-topic --config cleanup.policy=3Dcompact

6. Produce some dummy data to the topic
$ bin/kafka-console-producer.sh --broker-list localhost:9092 --topic test-t=
opic --property "parse.key=3Dtrue" --property "key.separator=3D:"


>key1:this is a test
>key2:another test

7. Verify that the logs have rolled over:
$ ls -l /tmp/kafka-logs/test-topic-0

8. Wait for 10 seconds (our log.retention.ms value) and change log.segment.=
bytes
$ bin/kafka-configs.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --entity-type brok=
ers --entity-default --alter --add-config log.segment.bytes=3D95

9. Consume the data from the topic:
$  % bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topi=
c test-topic --from-beginning
# Output should be:
> this is a test
> another test

9. Wait for at least 10 seconds and change it again:
$ bin/kafka-configs.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --entity-type brok=
ers --entity-default --alter --add-config log.segment.bytes=3D105

10. 9. Consume the data from the topic:
$ % bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic=
 test-topic --from-beginning=20
# Output is empty now
> {code}
Even though this leads to {*}loss of data{*}, I am not marking it as Critic=
al because the Kafka version this affects is quite old.

=C2=A0



