Shivsundar R created KAFKA-17502:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Modify handling of commitSync() in ShareConsumeReques=
tManager
                 Key: KAFKA-17502
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17502
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
            Reporter: Shivsundar R


Currently the code in ShareConsumeRequestManager works on the basis that th=
ere can only be one commitSync()/close() at a time. But there is a chance t=
hese calls timeout on the application thread, but are still sent later on t=
he background thread.
To cover this case, we will now have a list of AcknowledgeRequestStates to =
store the commitSyncs() and a separate requestState to store the close().

=C2=A0



--
