Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-17575) TestUtils.tempDirectory registers
 two shutdown hooks for the same thing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Stig Rohde D=C3=B8ssing created KAFKA-17575:
------------------------------------------

             Summary: TestUtils.tempDirectory registers two shutdown hooks =
for the same thing
                 Key: KAFKA-17575
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17575
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Stig Rohde D=C3=B8ssing


TestUtils.tempDirectory registers a shutdown hook to clean up the temporary=
 file/directory on JVM exit. But it also calls file.deleteOnExit, which ess=
entially does the same thing. There's no reason to do both, setting up a sh=
utdown hook via Exit.addShutdownHook should be good enough.



