hi David

The two-tiered approach is interesting and I have questions similar to
TengYao.

BUT, go back to the usage of quarantine and isolation. It seems to me they
are used to make our CI not be noised by the flaky, right? If so, could we
query the Gradle develocity to get flaky and then make only those flaky
retryable in CI? That means a non-flaky (stable) test must pass without
retry.

This approach is more simple (I guess), and it can isolate the flaky (by
retry) from CI. If a flaky can't pass after retry, I feel it is a critical
failed test rather than just a flaky. On top of that, this approach does
not need an extra file ("quarantined.txt") in git control and it does not
need to change any code of test classes.

Best,
Chia-Ping

