utomatically
> placing a new test into the quarantine will allow us to observe its
> behavior without the risk of failing builds. After a few days of successf=
ul
> runs, these tests will graduate from the quarantine and be run as part of
> the main suite. =E2=80=9D
>
> It seems those new tests will be placed into quarantine automatically.
>
> However, the next description: =E2=80=9C Placing a new test into the quar=
antine
> will be made at the discretion of the PR authors and/or committers. It
> should not be compulsory.=E2=80=9D
>
> It seems it is up to authors and/or committers.
>
>
> Q1:
>
> Could you please share more details about =E2=80=9C Placing a new test in=
to the
> quarantine=E2=80=9D? Do you mean =E2=80=9Cadd the flaky annotation to the=
 new integration
> tests in the PR=E2=80=9D?
>
>
> Q2:
>
> Are the quarantine tests included by PR=E2=80=99s CI? If yes, could we (c=
ommitters
> and author) ignore the failure of quarantine tests? If not, should we
