hi David

> For instance, we could check whether the member id is already used and we
could regenerate another one if it is. However, I tend to believe that the
risk of collision within a group is neglectable.

I agree the risk is negligible when the member ID is generated by the
server, as we can always ensure the server behaves responsibly. =F0=9F=98=
=80
Therefore, I don't believe the additional check for the member ID is
necessary if the member id is created by server.

However, my concern is that consumers are now required to generate the
member ID, so as a responsible server, we need to handle the incorrect
client behavior. At least, based on David's comment, we can create another
member id when it is already used and it is rejoining the group (member
epoch =3D 0).

By the way, another related issue is that a duplicate consumer may
inadvertently terminate another consumer, as it will always send a
LEAVE_GROUP request upon closing, even if it hasn't received a heartbeat
response. However, I tend to believe the risk is negligible =F0=9F=98=80

Best,
Chia-Ping


