Hi Chia-Ping,

> However, my concern is that consumers are now required to generate the
member ID, so as a responsible server, we need to handle the incorrect
client behavior. At least, based on David's comment, we can create another
member id when it is already used and it is rejoining the group (member
epoch =3D 0).

I don't disagree with the concern. However, I don't see how we could make
it work in practice. Let's say that a member XYZ sends a heartbeat with
epoch zero. The server cannot know whether it is a new member joining for
the first time or an existing member rejoining because it was fenced (e.g.
wrong epoch, session timed out, etc.). We cannot differentiate the two
cases. Hence we cannot handle it on the server side. The only viable
alternative is to keep the member id generation on the server side if we
are concerned by clients not able to generate unique uuids on their side. I
tend to believe that generating a uuid on the client should not be that
difficult so I am not too concerned about it. How do you see
this, Chia-Ping?

Cheers,
David

