>> In my opinion, the main concern is that non-trunk PRs can't effectively
>> leverage the cache, meaning they require more time and resources to run
>> CI.
>> Additionally, github-ci is triggered by trunk branch only, and we have n=
ot
>> tested it on non-trunk branch yet. Given that 3.9.0 and 3.8.1 releases a=
re
