Subject: Re: [DISCUSS] KIP-1092: Extend Consumer#close with an option to leave
 the group or not
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary="0000000000007c059806230fad40"

--0000000000007c059806230fad40
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

> I think I=E2=80=99m actually OK with leaving it as leaveGroup with a lot =
of
documentation that warns users away from changing it arbitrarily.

Pardon me, I just want to ensure we are all on the same page.

   1. `leaveGroup=3Dtrue`:  `ClassicKafkaConsumer` sends a
   `LeaveGroupRequest` for either the dynamic or static member.
   2. `leaveGroup=3Dfalse`:  `ClassicKafkaConsumer` does not send any `
   LeaveGroupRequest` for either the dynamic or static member.
   3. `leaveGroup=3Ddefault` (current behavior): `ClassicKafkaConsumer` sen=
ds
   a `LeaveGroupRequest` for dynamic member, and it does NOT send any
   `ConsumerGroupHeartbeatRequest`for static member
   4. `leaveGroup=3Dtrue`:  `AsyncKafkaConsumer` sends a
   `ConsumerGroupHeartbeatRequest` with "-1" epoch for either the dynamic o=
r
   static member
   5. `leaveGroup=3Dfalse`: `AsyncKafkaConsumer` sends a
   `ConsumerGroupHeartbeatRequest` with "-2" epoch for the static member, a=
nd
   it does NOT send any `ConsumerGroupHeartbeatRequest` for dynamic member
   6. `leaveGroup=3Ddefault` (current behavior): `AsyncKafkaConsumer` sends=
 a
   `ConsumerGroupHeartbeatRequest`with "-1" epoch for dynamic member and
   "-2" epoch for static member

Best,
Chia-Ping

