Hi, we are evaluating the Kafka Tiered Storage. We already see KAFKA-17062 =
which under 3.9 we could have data loss. I was looking at the code and also=
 the KIP-405.=C2=A0

=C2=A0

On the KIP it is mentioned that if a copy fails it will be retried with a b=
ackoff propagation defined on REMOTE_LOG_MANAGER_TASK_RETRY_BACK_OFF_MS_PRO=
P.=C2=A0 The issue is the method=C2=A0 remoteLogManagerTaskRetryBackoffMs()=
 is not used in any place of the code. So I think this parameters make no e=
ffect currently. Is there any retry of failed segments ? Until now I just s=
aw logging the error.

Question from me:=C2=A0 What happen to segments that have the state=C2=A0 C=
OPY_SEGMENT_STARTED between server restarts?

