Kevin Fletcher created KAFKA-17666:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Kafka doesn't monitor disk space after it detects it =
is full
                 Key: KAFKA-17666
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17666
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Kevin Fletcher


Scenario: Kafka data volume becomes full (100%) but once freed up, Kafka ig=
nores this disk until it is restarted. It does not auto-detect that space h=
as been freed up, and begin to function again, without restarting.
{code:java}
Sep 12 17:40:39 kq-2b.was2.sd.com kafka-server-start[1696]: Stopping servin=
g replicas in dir /opt/clusterone/kafka/disk4 (kafka.server.ReplicaManager)
...
