Issue 1: After freeing up disk space (or growing a volume in real-time), Ka=
fka never reports any further log msgs about disk4, it just ignores it unti=
l it is restarted.

It would be ideal if Kafka could periodicially check back on this disk and =
see if it is freed up yet so it can continue.

Issue 2: When shrinking retention live (via retention.ms for example), Kafk=
a does not begin to delete files from the 100% full disk, instead it contin=
ues to ignore all activity related to disk4. This forces us to have to manu=
ally delete files from the disk (less than ideal).

